(FIL-32: the three open modes behave as documented: reading opens an existing file, writing creates/overwrites (truncating), appending adds to the end.
 Also covers: FIL-33, FIL-34, FIL-41.
 "0123456789" is overwritten by "AB" (truncate), then "-appended" is added:
 11 bytes, not 19, is the proof that writing truncated.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-32.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   AB-appended
   11
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called output at "vf_scratch/files/modes.txt".
Write "0123456789" to output.
Close output.
open a file for writing called 'the overwriter' at "vf_scratch/files/modes.txt".
Write "AB" to 'the overwriter'.
Close 'the overwriter'.
open a file for appending called log at "vf_scratch/files/modes.txt".
Write "-appended" to log.
Close log.
open a file for reading called source at "vf_scratch/files/modes.txt".
a buffer called contents is 64 bytes in size.
Read from source into contents.
print contents.
print contents's size.
Close source.
